// Local-development-only Go workspace. It makes downstream-bff resolve
// backend-v2 from source in this checkout instead of fetching a published
// module version, so the two can be iterated on together before backend-v2
// has ever cut a release. It does NOT affect either module's own go.mod/
// go.sum — CI and any real downstream consumer builds each module normally
// (`GOWORK=off go build ./...` from within a module dir, or simply not
// having a go.work file), resolving backend-v2 the real way: a pinned,
// tagged, checksummed version. See backend-v2/README.md and
// downstream-bff/README.md for the full versioning story.
go 1.26.5

use (
	./backend-v2
	./downstream-bff
)
